00:44:37.660 --> 00:44:40.970
<v One Of The Hens>Everybody in here [UNINTELLIGIBLE PHRASE].
<v One Of The Hens>这里的每个人[听不清短语]。

00:44:40.970 --> 00:44:55.620
<v Ira  Glass>The Hens-- Tiny, Lynn and Jewel in the studio. Also, Barbara, Rosetta, Valerie, Sally, Tony and Jan. This next song is the song that they always play driving home from their trips when they have to return to their husbands and kids and real life.
<v Ira  Glass>“母鸡们”——泰妮、琳和朱厄尔在演播室。还有芭芭拉、罗塞塔、瓦莱丽、萨莉、托尼和简。下一首歌是她们每次旅行归家，不得不回到丈夫、孩子和现实生活中时，在车里总是播放的歌。

00:44:55.620 --> 00:45:16.520
<v Ira  Glass>[MUSIC- "BACK TO LIFE" BY SOUL II SOUL]
<v Ira  Glass>[音乐- Soul II Soul的《Back to Life》]

00:45:16.520 --> 00:45:22.750
<v Ira Glass>Act Four, Taking Sisterhood One Step Further.
<v Ira Glass>第四幕，将姐妹情谊更进一步。

00:45:22.750 --> 00:45:30.360
<v Ira Glass>If you ask Elizabeth Joseph, it was the only reasonable choice to marry a man who was already married to five women. She met her husband when she was a senior in college.
<v Ira Glass>如果你问伊丽莎白·约瑟夫（Elizabeth Joseph），嫁给一个已经娶了五个妻子的男人是唯一的合理选择。她在大学四年级时遇到了她的丈夫。

00:45:30.360 --> 00:46:02.080
<v Elizabeth Joseph>Well, you look at somebody in my situation. I was almost 21 years old. I could either marry somebody my own age and take another 10 years and finish the job of raising him, his mother started. Or I could marry a proven failure and I practice divorce law. I know there's all kinds of wonderful excuses for divorce, but by definition it's a failure. Or I could have found myself somebody who had proven himself to be a good husband, but maybe I didn't want to marry a 65-year-old widower.
<v Elizabeth Joseph>嗯，你看看我的情况。我快21岁了。我可以嫁给一个同龄人，再花10年时间完成他母亲开始的抚养工作。或者我可以嫁给一个公认的失败者，我是做离婚法的。我知道关于离婚有各种各样的美妙借口，但根据定义，这就是失败。或者我可以找一个证明自己是个好丈夫的人，但我可能不想嫁给一个65岁的鳏夫。

00:46:02.080 --> 00:46:10.810
<v Elizabeth Joseph>So in Alex, there was no gamble. He was demonstrably a good husband, demonstrably a good father. So there was little risk to the situation.
<v Elizabeth Joseph>所以在亚历克斯（Alex）身上，没有赌博。他显然是个好丈夫，显然是个好父亲。所以这种情况几乎没有风险。

00:46:10.810 --> 00:46:30.690
<v Ira Glass>Elizabeth Joseph is as an attorney and now public affairs director of a radio station in Utah. We offer her story as part of our show as another example in the continuum of how to be a woman or a girl. She says that because she was in a polygamist marriage, she could do things like go off to law school and finish school and not have to worry who was taking care of the kids or her husband. There were other wives around for that.
<v Ira Glass>伊丽莎白·约瑟夫是一位律师，现在是犹他州一家广播电台的公共事务主管。我们将她的故事作为节目的一部分，作为关于如何做女人或女孩的连续体中的另一个例子。她说，因为她是一夫多妻婚姻，她可以做些事，比如去法学院完成学业，而不必担心是谁在照顾孩子或丈夫。还有其他妻子在照顾这些事。

00:46:30.690 --> 00:46:33.630
<v Ira Glass>In short, she says, polygamy is the ultimate feminist lifestyle.
<v Ira Glass>总之，她说，一夫多妻制是终极的女性主义生活方式。

00:46:33.630 --> 00:47:11.220
<v Elizabeth Joseph>It's having a man on your own terms. You know, he's in your bed. He's in your house at your invitation. The juggling act that so many women have to put on with respect to careers and family is so much relieved in our situation because there are so many of us to share those kinds of household duties and child rearing and husband taking care of. So I'm able to go to work with a guilt free heart and child never sees the inside of a daycare center or anything like that. They're home with people who care about them.
<v Elizabeth Joseph>这是按照你自己的条件拥有一个男人。你知道，他应你的邀请在你的床上、在你的家里。许多女性在职业和家庭之间不得不进行的杂耍式努力，在我们的情况下减轻了许多，因为我们有很多人来分担那种家务和育儿、照顾丈夫的工作。所以我能带着无罪恶感的心去工作，孩子永远看不到日托中心的内部，诸如此类。他们和照顾他们的人在一起。

00:47:11.220 --> 00:47:13.280
<v Ira Glass>Now your husband has eight wives?
<v Ira Glass>现在你有八个妻子？

00:47:13.280 --> 00:47:15.950
<v Elizabeth Joseph>Yes.
<v Elizabeth Joseph>是的。

00:47:15.950 --> 00:47:21.310
<v Ira Glass>And how many of the wives actually stay home? Do all of them work? Do just some of them work?
<v Ira Glass>有多少个妻子实际上待在家里？她们都工作吗？只有一些工作？

00:47:21.310 --> 00:47:44.220
<v Elizabeth Joseph>Yeah, we all work. We all work. About nine years ago three of us had babies all in the same year and there was one wife in particular that we really wanted to watch out for the kids while we were at work. And so we went to her and said how much is it going to take to get you to quit your job for a couple of years til the kids go to school? So she did that for us. Then she went back to work.
<v Elizabeth Joseph>是的，我们都工作。我们都工作。大约九年前，我们三个同一年生了孩子，特别有一个妻子我们真的很想让她在上班时照看孩子。所以我们去找她，说要给多少钱你才愿意辞掉工作几年，直到孩子上学？所以她为我们做了这件事。然后她又回去工作了。

00:47:44.220 --> 00:47:47.200
<v Ira Glass>And when you say, how much would it take you, did the rest of you pay her?
<v Ira Glass>当你问要多少钱时，你们其余的人付给她了吗？

00:47:47.200 --> 00:47:48.810
<v Elizabeth Joseph>Yeah, the three of us paid her.
<v Elizabeth Joseph>是的，我们三个付给她。

00:47:48.810 --> 00:47:49.630
<v Ira Glass>Wow.
<v Ira Glass>哇。

00:47:49.630 --> 00:47:51.370
<v Elizabeth Joseph>It was only fair, she was working hard.
<v Elizabeth Joseph>这很公平，她工作很努力。

00:47:51.370 --> 00:47:58.360
<v Ira Glass>So when you first met your husband, had you been considering polygamy as an option?
<v Ira Glass>所以当你第一次见到你丈夫时，你有考虑过一夫多妻制作为一种选择吗？

00:47:58.360 --> 00:48:16.690
<v Elizabeth Joseph>Oh, only very recently because a friend of his had proposed to me also. But no, I didn't even know it existed when I was in college until I met my husband and his friend. I had no idea anybody was doing it modernly. I was aware of the LDS history of the last century.
<v Elizabeth Joseph>哦，那是非常近期的事，因为他的一个朋友也向我求婚了。但没有，我在大学时甚至不知道它的存在，直到我遇见我丈夫和他的朋友。我不知道有人在现代还这样做。我意识到了上个世纪的后期耶稣基督后期圣徒教会（LDS）的历史。

00:48:16.690 --> 00:48:26.230
<v Ira Glass>The Mormon church, the Latter Day Saints Church? And when you met him, he was already married to five women at that point, right?
<v Ira Glass>摩门教，后期圣徒教会？当你见到他时，他当时已经娶了五个妻子，对吗？

00:48:26.230 --> 00:48:27.410
<v Elizabeth Joseph>Correct.
<v Elizabeth Joseph>对。

00:48:27.410 --> 00:48:30.730
<v Ira Glass>How did a courtship happen? Like what actually happened?
<v Ira Glass>求爱是怎么发生的？到底发生了什么？

00:48:30.730 --> 00:48:53.350
<v Elizabeth Joseph>Well, we were separated by a thousand miles. He proposed by letter. And I flew down and spent my spring break my senior year with him and his family. He had married two of my best friends from college. So I came I thought as much to see them as him. But I just needed to check out the situation. And I went home married.
<v Elizabeth Joseph>嗯，我们相隔千里。他是通过信件求婚的。我飞过去，在他和他的家人那里度过了我大四的春假。他娶了我在大学里的两个好朋友。所以我去的时候，我想看她们和看他一样重要。但我只是需要审视一下情况。然后我结婚回家了。

00:48:53.350 --> 00:48:55.700
<v Ira  Glass>What did your family say?
<v Ira  Glass>你的家人怎么说？

